3. How a Browser Requests and Displays a Web Page (Step-by-Step)

User enters a URL in the browser.

The browser converts the domain (example.com) to an IP using DNS.

A HTTP/HTTPS request is sent to the server.

The server receives the request and finds the required file.

The server sends the HTML, CSS, JS back to the browser.

The browser parses the HTML and builds:

DOM (Document Object Model) from HTML

CSSOM (CSS Object Model) from CSS

Browser combines DOM + CSSOM → Render Tree.

JavaScript is executed to add interactivity.

Page is displayed.
